# constraint_trait_rejected.tkr — the SM-G12 (crumb 0018) sole-rejected-term anchor: after the
# term grammar broadens to a full type (named/slice/error/disjunction/form/lifetime/interface), a
# trait is the ONE term still refused — a trait is a concrete mixin, never a type.

Feature: constraint_trait_rejected — a trait is the sole rejected constraint term

  Scenario: trait_in_constraint_rejected — a trait constrains a type parameter, but a trait is not a type
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "cannot appear in a constraint"
